From 5d7fa3299fdcfb09f7d395b5f0881387c595c226 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 19:10:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04/79] demux: tta: allow seeking to the start

DEMUX_SET_POSITION computes a byte target from the requested position and
then acts on it only when it is strictly positive, so position 0 - which
is how the input rewinds a file in order to repeat it, and where the seek
bar's left edge lands - was rejected with VLC_EGENERIC every time.

Nothing below needs the target to be non-zero: the seek table walk starts
at frame 0 with an accumulator of 0 and stops immediately, which is the
right answer. Accept it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 modules/demux/tta.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/modules/demux/tta.c b/modules/demux/tta.c
index bf1ea54438..a79a7f528e 100644
--- a/modules/demux/tta.c
+++ b/modules/demux/tta.c
@@ -251,7 +251,10 @@ static int Control( demux_t *p_demux, int i_query, va_list args )
         case DEMUX_SET_POSITION:
             f = va_arg( args, double );
             i64 = (int64_t)(f * (stream_Size( p_demux->s ) - p_sys->i_start));
-            if( i64 > 0 )
+            /* Position 0 is a valid target and lands on the first frame; the
+             * loop below copes with it. Rejecting it made seeking back to the
+             * start - which is how a file is repeated - always fail. */
+            if( i64 >= 0 )
             {
                 int64_t tmp = 0;
                 uint32_t i;
